{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018v6vPH5AJemLRwrrDcpmwt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W82kypC3573rcYcsGHJNP6","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"claude","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 in a full-mode dream paper review. Your focus is **Methods + Experiments**. Do NOT evaluate novelty or related work (that's Reviewer 2's job). Do NOT evaluate formatting.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: Classification vs. Generation for Execution Simulation: A Complexity-Dependent Analysis of Code Verification Formulations\n\n**Core proposal**: Per-test binary classification (ExecCLS) as a third formulation for execution-free code patch verification, alongside trajectory-level scoring (SWE-RM) and Code World Models (CWM/generation). Given (code_patch, test), the model outputs a single token: pass or fail.\n\n**Method (Section 3)**:\n- Three formulations compared: ExecCLS (binary classification, 1 token output), CWM (generation of full execution output, 1-4096+ tokens), trajectory-level (full candidate context, single resolved/unresolved label)\n- Fine-tune Qwen3-4B and Qwen3-8B with LoRA (rank 64, α=128) on each formulation\n- Function-level training data: HumanEval/MBPP with execution-derived labels\n- Repo-level: Construct SWE-bench-PerTest (438 instances from 500 SWE-bench Verified, 16 candidate patches each, ~54K training samples, 350 train / 88 eval)\n- Evaluation: Pass F1, Fail F1, overall accuracy; 3 seeds {0,1,42}; paired bootstrap + McNemar's test\n\n**Key Results**:\n- Table 1: Function-level CLS vs CWM: 87.4±0.46 vs 87.4±0.56 accuracy, p=0.72 (null result)\n- Table 2: Trace-then-judge ablation: 87.8% vs 87.4% direct CLS (negligible difference)\n- Table 3: Scale analysis: both scale equally 4B→8B (~2pp gain), gap stays near zero\n- Table 4: Per-test CLS outperforms trajectory-level by 4.2pp (87.4 vs 83.2)\n- Table 5: Repo-level: CLS 75.5% vs CWM 73.0% at 4B (2.5pp gap); CWM has 8.7% unparseable + 3.2% truncated = 11.9% failure rate; at 8B: CLS 78.3% vs CWM 75.9% (2.4pp gap, 7.9% failure)\n- Table 6: Summary — function-level gap=0.0, repo-level gap=2.5\n- Table 7: Fine-tuned 4B CLS (75.5%) outperforms 32B zero-shot (71.5% traj, 68.3% per-test) at ~10× lower cost\n- Table 8: Oracle per-test advantage by F2P count: T=1 (68.7% of instances) → IID Adv 0.020; T≥2 (31.3%) → meaningful advantage\n- Table 9: Empirical error correlation ρ=0.21, placing realistic advantage at ~10pp for multi-test instances\n- Table 10: Re-repair: +1.5pp resolve rate improvement, p=0.18, CI [-0.7, 3.7]\n- Table 11: Per-test prediction quality by difficulty: easy Fail F1=0.93, hard Fail F1=0.78\n- Table 12: Majority voting K=3: 88.7% vs 87.4% (+1.3pp at 3× cost)\n\n**This is a \"median\" tier dream paper.**\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate along these dimensions:\n1. **Method description**: Is it complete? Are claims supported by experimental data? Are key hyperparameters / training procedures clear?\n2. **Experimental design**: Does it cover key baselines / ablations / cross-dataset / scale dimensions?\n3. **Data presentation**: Can a reviewer reproduce conclusions from tables/figures? Are error bars / statistical significance sufficient?\n\nIdentify:\n- Major issues (would affect accept/reject decision)\n- Minor issues (should be addressed but not deal-breakers)\n- Strengths\n\nBe specific with table/section references. Provide your assessment as: strong reject / borderline reject / borderline / borderline accept / weak accept / accept.\n\nWrite your review in a structured format. Be thorough but concise."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3013,"cache_read_input_tokens":34493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3013},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c605f9c-e8db-4550-af65-fae2c810322a","uuid":"2fa69462-6737-4f89-9738-b71ca603ceb5"}
